762abd7c85562812","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/social-content/SKILL.md","size":21040,"sha256":"9c40b9ceda9094b3ce256d62ca8a33e8f82f323cff357da294e14262ed429b69","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":3945,"sha256":"e48a24aab0268c4b2e0b63f537eca86c8cb417bd6efd9ca3e0f93d94ba5a0951","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016896436,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bb1fc1df45942a8da72a0a0c7160a821023d8cf02f6eb8d066df5ebff121679e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bb1fc1df45942a8da72a0a0c7160a821023d8cf02f6eb8d066df5ebff121679e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: marketing-skills\nVersion: 0.1.2\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle 'marketing-skills' is benign. All files contain extensive, well-structured documentation and advice on various marketing topics. External URLs mentioned are for legitimate, well-known marketing tools or official documentation (e.g., Google Analytics, Optimizely, Product Hunt). Code snippets (e.g., JavaScript for analytics, JSON-LD for schema) are presented as examples for the user to implement, not as code for the AI agent to execute. There is no evidence of prompt injection, malicious execution, data exfiltration, persistence, or obfuscation. The instructions consistently align with the stated purpose of providing marketing expertise.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159819775},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":26,"checkedAt":1789016896436},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a Markdown-only marketing playbook, but some modules claim direct ad/social account access and include broad scraping or data-collection guidance without strong approval boundaries.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Marketing analytics, lead capture, customer-list uploads, retargeting, and social scraping can be purpose-aligned, but the artifact under-specifies privacy, consent, platform-terms, and account-action controls in some modules.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact contains Markdown skill files only; no executable install scripts, dependencies, remote payload retrieval, or static-scan findings were present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Several module triggers are broad, and the high-impact ad/social modules do not set clear draft-only defaults, confirmation steps, or approval boundaries before spend-affecting or public-posting actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No system persistence, privilege escalation, background worker, local credential-store access, or memory-writing behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The main purpose is coherent marketing guidance, but paid-ads and social-content expand from advisory playbooks into claimed direct access to ad accounts and social scheduling/publishing platforms.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want marketing advisory content, and keep connected ad accounts, social schedulers, customer-list uploads, analytics identifiers, and scraping tools behind explicit user approval. Require preview of exact posts, accounts, times, budgets, audiences, and data sources before any action, and review privacy law, consent, and platform terms before using tracking, retargeting, lead capture, or scraping guidance.","findings":"[P6] expected: The cited text is ordinary module output guidance and paywall re-display terminology; I found no instruction to reveal system prompts or hidden rules.\n[OH1] expected: The cited React snippet is a JSON-LD schema rendering pattern using JSON.stringify; it would benefit from validation guidance but is not evidence of arbitrary command or HTML injection by the skill itself.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Broad activation language is mostly a routing-quality issue, but it becomes material where it can surface modules that claim direct ad-account or social-publishing access.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The social-content module says the agent has direct access to a platform that publishes to major social networks, without explicit draft-only mode or per-post user confirmation.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The social-content module recommends collecting 500-1000+ posts with scraping and automation tools, which is broader than needed for ordinary content help and lacks platform-terms and privacy constraints.\n[SQP-2] expected: Analytics identifiers and lead capture are expected in marketing implementation guidance, and the analytics module does include later privacy and no-PII checks, though some capture guidance remains under-scoped.\n[TM3] expected: The GA4 debug_mode reference is a testing/debugging instruction, not an unsafe security default.\n[EA2] expected: The phrase 'no confirmation' refers to avoiding a duplicate email-confirmation form field, not autonomous execution of a high-impact action.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016896436}}}}}